From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme, win32u, userenv, shell32, gdi32: theme frame options, Group Policy notification, notification state, CancelDC

Stubs that said yes and did nothing, as documented now:

- SetWindowThemeAttribute(WTA_NONCLIENT) (E_NOTIMPL): the WTA_OPTIONS
  flags, set through their mask, are kept on the window and win32u's frame
  drawing and hit testing follow them: WTNCA_NODRAWCAPTION leaves out the
  caption text, WTNCA_NODRAWICON the icon, WTNCA_NOSYSMENU the system menu
  (the icon's place is caption). Other types or sizes: E_INVALIDARG. The
  frame is redrawn. uxtheme.h gets WTA_OPTIONS and the WTNCA_ flags.
- RegisterGPNotification (said TRUE, never signalled): the event is set
  when the machine's or the user's Software\Policies key changes (policy
  is applied by writing it) and when RefreshPolicy asks for a refresh;
  UnregisterGPNotification takes it back. RefreshPolicy and
  RefreshPolicyEx (RP_FORCE) are added.
- EnterCriticalPolicySection (ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED) and
  LeaveCriticalPolicySection: a named mutex per machine and user, waited
  for up to ten minutes, as documented.
- SHQueryUserNotificationState (always QUNS_ACCEPTS_NOTIFICATIONS):
  QUNS_NOT_PRESENT while the screen saver runs or the input desktop is
  locked away, QUNS_BUSY with a full-screen window in front (not the
  desktop or the shell's windows), QUNS_QUIET_TIME when notifications from
  apps are turned off (NOC_GLOBAL_SETTING_TOASTS_ENABLED = 0).
- CancelDC: drawing is done at once in the calling thread here, so there
  is nothing pending to cancel; it now answers whether hdc is a device
  context (ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE) instead of always TRUE.

Gate: test/shellmisc-gate.sh (test/shellmisc-probe.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_WTA (win32u/defwnd.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_GP_NOTIFY
(userenv/userenv_main.c), SG_MUTANT_ALWAYS_ACCEPTS (shell32/shell32_main.c).
---
